<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Baranov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1747">1747</a>–<a href="/years/1819">1819</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Baranov was a Russian merchant who managed the Russian fur-trading posts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a> from 1790 and became the first chief manager of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-american-company">Russian-American Company</a> in 1799. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sitka">New Archangel</a>, present-day Sitka, which became the capital of Russian America after it was retaken from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlingit">Tlingit</a> in 1804, and governed the colony until 1818.</p></div>
